# Everything this repository ignores, in one file (dbmeta D58).

# The upstream tree-sitter checkout. It is a reference for the port, and it is
# never part of this repository. See D4 and docs/UPSTREAM.md. The rule has no
# slash at its end, so it also matches a symbolic link to the checkout in a git
# worktree (D86).
/tree-sitter

# The Claude Code permissions of one person. The shared .claude/settings.json
# is not ignored, because a setting that belongs to the project is committed.
# See dbmeta D89.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The git worktrees in which the coding agents work. Each one is a checkout of
# this repository, and its work comes back through the main checkout.
/.claude/worktrees/
